{
 "_doc": "The campaign's data (openspec/changes/game-flow-engine): factions, sector terrain, hulls by tier, ship systems and supplies, the rules' numbers, and the map (its territory seeds; its star systems, each a star with its belt of asteroids at belt_r sectors, a share of that ring taken, and a nebula of that many sectors beside it; the deep space between them, dust clouds and asteroid fields with no star, clear_of_stars sectors from any; how far your fleet and friendly ships see; ports, fleets and freight routes). A planet with no star within 3 sectors is a rogue planet. The one copy the game and the campaign mockup (docs/mockups/game-flow.html, inlined by tools/mockups/inline_data.py) read. Missions are in data/missions/. Prices are points; the campaign charges points x credit_rate credits. Hulls: each faction's by tier (1 the smallest); battle_class is the ship class it fights as (data/battle/classes.json), schematic its top-down picture (assets/ships/schematics/), empty while the hull is a stand-in. Supplies: at most one per hp_per hull points, per_fit per fitted system fit, or fixed. Freighters (openspec/changes/freighter-missions; owner, 2026-11-07): each faction's freighter is the hull its 'freighter' names (the faction's own approved freighter, mockup 24; a faction with none flies the neutral 'freighter' stand-in); freighter hulls are neutral and never for sale. Ships do not mend between battles: a hull is repaired at your own port (repair_share of its price) or in the field with a repair kit (the parts supply), each mending kit_repair_pct of the hull. A freighter destroyed or taken is off its route for freighter_refit_turns turns.",
